{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor ultimately recognized the combined wound and diabetes danger, changed from conditional short-interval clinic follow-up to same-day hospital evaluation, and the caregiver executed the handoff to the original surgical hospital. The plan avoided unsupported home medication changes after escalation, directed hospital-managed insulin/metformin decisions, and preserved emergency/onsite escalation thresholds. Two high-order points were completed with meaningful impact: practical offline-path navigation and dynamic reprioritization after drainage/odor, low-grade temperature, and glucose 18.6 emerged. No responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect remains in the bounded episode, supporting grade 5.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00182",
        "explanation": "Doctor endorsed the current episode decision to remain under hospital observation/admission and wait for onsite orders.",
        "quote": "同意住院/留观安排"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00196",
        "explanation": "Caregiver confirmed the handoff was executed and hospital team had taken over treatment.",
        "quote": "现在人被安排到留观床/病区床这边了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The pre-handoff episode reached a safe handoff: the patient was at the original hospital/observation area, with IV access, glucose and dressing monitoring, and instructions not to self-administer home diabetes medications. Remaining uncertainties such as culture results, exact inpatient orders, and possible surgery were appropriately left to the onsite team.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
